infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Why dedup is probabilistic: exact set vs bloom filter
  desc Remembering 10 billion seen URLs — the number that shapes the architecture
  compares
    - label Exact in-memory set
      children
        - label ~100 bytes per URL
          desc Full URL string stored
        - label ~1 TB of RAM
          desc 10 billion seen URLs, exact
        - label Zero skipped pages
          desc No false positives or negatives
        - label Unaffordable at web scale
          desc Cost rules it out
    - label Bloom filter
      children
        - label A few bits per URL
          desc Bit array, not the string
        - label ~100x less memory
          desc Fits in RAM
        - label No false negatives
          desc "Not seen" means truly new
        - label Tunable false positives
          desc Rarely skips a new URL — harmless
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
